{
  "info": {
    "name": "paccradle API: skeleton, surfaces and versioning (2026-10-29)",
    "description": "Change: M1-D1, API skeleton (2026-10-29). New: the URL scheme, versioning, shared headers, the error body, and the first routes. Merge into the main contract.\n\n## URL scheme\nEvery route sits on one surface, each with its own routes, CORS origin, sign-in and contract version:\n\n| Surface | Prefix | Caller | Version |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| client | `/api/client/v1` | the web app's users | 1.0.0-beta.1 |\n| admin | `/api/admin/v1` | the back office (signed-in admins only) | 1.0.0-beta.1 |\n| probes | `/healthz`, `/readyz` | deploy scripts, uptime checks | not versioned |\n\nPaths are lower case, plural nouns for collections, `snake_case` for JSON fields and query parameters (e.g. `/api/client/v1/designs/{design_id}/exports`). Paddle's webhook will sit at `/api/webhooks/v1/paddle` (M1-F).\n\n## Versioning (semver, per surface)\n- The URL holds the major version; the `api-version` response header holds the full one.\n- Patch: a fix, no shape change. Minor: something callers can ignore (new endpoint, optional field, response field, error code). Major: anything that can break a caller; it gets a new prefix (`/v2`) and the old one keeps running until callers move.\n- `1.0.0-beta.N` until the public launch (M2): the web app is the only caller, so the contract may still change; each change bumps N and gets a dated file like this one.\n\n## Headers on every response\n- `x-request-id`: UUID v7 made by the API (one sent by the caller is ignored). Show it in error messages.\n- `api-version`: the surface's contract version (not on probes).\n- `retry-after`: seconds, on 429.\n- Bodies are gzip or brotli compressed when the request allows it, except responses that set a cookie.\n\n## Request headers\n- `Accept-Language`: language of error messages. English only for now; anything else falls back to English.\n- CORS: the client surface answers only `APP_WEB_URL`, the admin surface only `ADMIN_WEB_URL`; credentials allowed; preflights cached 10 minutes.\n\n## Errors\nEvery 4xx/5xx body: `{ \"error\": { \"code\", \"message\", \"meta\" } }`. Branch on `code`; `message` is in the caller's language; `meta` holds the message's values (often `{}`).\n\n| Code | Status | Meta |\n|---|---|---|\n| INVALID_REQUEST | 400 (or 422 from a body that doesn't fit) | |\n| AUTH_REQUIRED | 401 | |\n| FORBIDDEN | 403 | |\n| ROUTE_NOT_FOUND | 404 | |\n| METHOD_NOT_ALLOWED | 405, `allow` header lists the methods | |\n| PAYLOAD_TOO_LARGE | 413 (JSON bodies: 1 MiB) | |\n| UNSUPPORTED_MEDIA_TYPE | 415 | |\n| RATE_LIMITED | 429, with `retry-after` | `retry_after_seconds` |\n| INTERNAL_ERROR | 500 | |\n| SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE | 503 | |\n| REQUEST_TIMEOUT | 503 (after 30 s) | `timeout_seconds` |\n\n## Limits\n600 requests per minute per client address across the API (`RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE`), on top of Nginx's own.\n",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
